<%# Shown once, on whatever page an invited member first lands on, until they
    dismiss it. Four steps, in the order they'll happen to you. %>
<section class="onboarding">
  <form method="post" action="/onboarding/dismiss" class="dismiss">
    <%== csrf_tag("/onboarding/dismiss") %>
    <input type="hidden" name="to" value="<%= path %>">
    <button type="submit" class="link" aria-label="Dismiss this introduction">&times;</button>
  </form>

  <h2>How this works</h2>
  <ol class="how">
    <li><strong>Your watchlist is the pool.</strong> We read your public
        Letterboxd watchlist each day. Nothing else about your account is
        touched, and you never add films here.</li>
    <li><strong>A round opens and you get a ballot.</strong> A handful of films
        the club could watch, drawn from everyone's watchlists. Drag them into
        the order you want them, top being your first choice.</li>
    <li><strong>The round is over once all users vote.</strong> Once
        the last ballot is in, the rankings are tallied and the club has its
        film. You can change your ballot until the round is over.</li>
    <li><strong>Watch it, then log it on Letterboxd.</strong> That's how we know
        you're done — we check your diary every few hours, so it can take a
        little while to show up here. Once everyone has logged it, the next
        round opens.</li>
  </ol>
  <p class="dim">If your club draws from a fixed list rather than your watchlists, it skips
     anything one of you has already seen &mdash; but Letterboxd only tells us your 72 most
     recent. <a href="/settings#import">Import your watched.csv</a> and it'll know the rest.</p>
  <p class="dim">Stuck on a film nobody can get hold of? Once a round has landed
     on its film, anyone can vote to skip it, and once half the club has —
     two people at the least — the round ends there and the next one opens.</p>
</section>
